{
    "//": [
        "The v1 root export set of @arkade-os/swap, and where each name went in v2.",
        "",
        "This file is the RECORD; `src/index.ts` and `src/protocol.ts` are the",
        "EXECUTION, and `test/exports.test.ts` diffs one against the other and fails on",
        "any name in one and not the other. It is not a list anyone maintains by hand:",
        "`scripts/export-inventory.mjs` re-derives the barrels from source, which is",
        "what stops this going stale the way the map it replaces did.",
        "",
        "S — stays on the root as part of the v2 surface.",
        "P — moved to `@arkade-os/swap/protocol` under an `@deprecated` pointer on the",
        "    declaration, and off the root in the same release. There is no window in",
        "    which a P name answers to both: 0.1.0 breaks against 0.1.0-rc.1 whatever",
        "    this barrel does, so root re-exports would have split one migration into",
        "    two and left 200 v1 names on a root whose claim is to be the v2 surface.",
        "    The subpath is a floor and not a staging area — nothing on it is",
        "    scheduled to be removed.",
        "I — internalized. The client owns the capability and the name is gone, with no",
        "    /protocol floor. I is a finding and not a default: it was taken only where",
        "    the entry consumer sweep found no import, and a later hit promotes a name",
        "    back to P.",
        "D — deleted outright, no floor. A vocabulary rather than a capability: keeping",
        "    it reachable would keep the misroute class the closed `Route` union exists",
        "    to end typed and constructible.",
        "R — the NAME stays on the root, bound to the v2 declaration; the v1",
        "    declaration behind it is dropped with no floor. Two names only, and the",
        "    reason this file needs a fifth letter the spec's four do not cover."
    ],
